 "method": "Each year's published median (B19013_001, in that survey year's dollars) is multiplied by CPI(2025) / CPI(year), where CPI is the annual average of the monthly BLS CPI-U for New York-Newark-Jersey City, all items, not seasonally adjusted (series CUURS12ASA0), averaged by this script from the monthly values. The published margin of error is scaled by the same factor. Peer values for 2025 are the published medians, unadjusted, since every city is measured in the same year's dollars; the 2025 peer values and the city's 2025 value are therefore directly comparable. Borough and race breakdowns are 2025 published medians. Citywide figures are for New York city (place 3651000); peers are matched on place GEOID (state + place FIPS) from data/peers.json; borough figures are the five counties.",
 "caveats": [
  "The deflator is the New York-area CPI-U, not the national price index the Census Bureau uses in its own historical income tables, so inflation-adjusted figures here will differ from Census Bureau reports.",
  "peer_series values are nominal (each year's own dollars), not inflation-adjusted, because a New York price index is wrong for other cities. 'New York' is included in peer_series in the same nominal dollars so the five lines can be compared with each other; do not plot it against the inflation-adjusted series.",
  "Race groups B (Black) and D (Asian) are race alone and include Hispanic members of those races; H is white alone, not Hispanic; I is Hispanic or Latino of any race.",
  "The ACS 1-year 2020 standard tables were never released (the Census Bureau published only experimental estimates because of pandemic data-collection problems), so 2020 is missing from every ACS series.",
  "The 2005 ACS covered only people in households; group quarters (dorms, prisons, nursing homes, shelters) were added in 2006. 2005 values are not strictly comparable to later years.",
  "All ACS figures are survey estimates. moe is the 90 percent margin of error, published by the Census Bureau for single cells and derived with the Bureau's approximation formulas for sums, shares and ratios.",
  "CPI annual averages are the mean of the months BLS published. Months with no published value: 2025 (M10 missing). BLS published no October 2025 index because prices were not collected during the 2025 federal government shutdown, so the 2025 average uses the 11 published months.",
  "2025 CPI annual average used as the base: 345.511 (1982-84=100)."
 ]
}
